t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119550 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b25256b2-09fe-5faa-b27a-bfea7654e8ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119550 #edb/ref 1074 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119551 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3020" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119551 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119551 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5c4164d7-605a-597c-9bab-f6599becc527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119551 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119552 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119552 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119552 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1d356bbb-b4ad-5730-9bd1-7f3cd151f96f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119552 #edb/ref 1074 "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119698 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8688" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119698 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119698 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40927582-03c4-5dcb-b2cc-7c68c73388b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119698 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1039 "Reversing the Limits of Integration" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119879 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119980 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119980 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119980 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119980 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 1759218626